In terms of group scheme actions, the above equivalences mean that the action of $\mathfrak{g}$ on $\spec(K)$ is free if and only if $[K:C]=p^e$, and if this action is free, then the corresponding quotient $\spec(C)=\spec(K)/\mathfrak{g}$ is a good quotient. Note that the general theorem about group scheme actions \cite[Thm 1(B), p. 112]{MuAbel} gives the left-to-right implication above.




