\begin{equation*}
\xymatrixcolsep{4pc}
\xymatrix{V \ar[d]_{\fr^m_V} \ar[r]^{}& V/\mathfrak{g} \ar[dl]_{\Psi}\\
	   V^{\fr^m} .  }
\end{equation*}
If $V=\spec(R)$ and $m=1$, then $\mathbf{R}$ is strict if and only if $\Psi$ is an isomorphism. It is also easy to see that for a reduced $R$ and arbitrary $m$,  $\mathbf{R}$ is strict if and only if $\Psi$ is an isomorphism.

