\begin{enumerate}
\item The extra property which makes the theory $F-\ddf$ nicer than the theory $\mathfrak{g}-\ddf$ is the existence of the \emph{smallest} strict extensions (Proposition \ref{strictext}). It gives the amalgamation property for \emph{all} (i.e. not necessarily strict) $F$-fields (Proposition \ref{apf}) and the quantifier elimination for $F-\dcf$.

\item In this context, quantifier elimination for $F-\dcf$ implies elimination of imaginaries for $F-\dcf$ exactly as in Section 4 of \cite{Zieg2}.
